</table>
</figure>
<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We list the details of each <span id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">MetaEmbed</span> variant in Table <a href="#A1.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ Appendix A Implementation Details ‣ MetaEmbed: Scaling Multimodal Retrieval at Test-Time with Flexible Late Interaction" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.
We reserve 1% training data from each subset of MMEB-train as evaluation split and training was early stopped when evaluation loss stops dropping.
All models are trained with gradient checkpointing <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen et al., 2016</a>)</cite> to reduce memory usage.
Training was conducted using PyTorch <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">Paszke et al., 2019</a>)</cite> <span id="A1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">2.6.0+cu124</span> and FlashAttention 2.0 <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dao, 2024</a>)</cite>.
For the 3B configuration, we adopt Distributed Data Parallel <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib37" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2020</a>)</cite> while for all other model sizes we use Fully Sharded Data Parallel (FSDP) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib72" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhao et al., 2023</a>)</cite> v2.
To prevent distributed hanging when training samples contain no images under FSDP, we pad those samples with a placeholder image to ensure the visual encoder is activated on each GPU.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
